{"id":875,"date":"2026-03-07T12:52:27","date_gmt":"2026-03-07T12:52:27","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:10005\/?p=875"},"modified":"2026-03-08T07:01:04","modified_gmt":"2026-03-08T07:01:04","slug":"%e5%9f%ba%e4%ba%8e%e5%b0%84%e9%a2%91%e6%8c%87%e7%ba%b9%e7%9a%84%e7%9c%9f%e5%ae%9e%e5%9c%ba%e6%99%af%e9%a3%9e%e6%9c%ba%e8%af%86%e5%88%ab%ef%bc%9a%e5%b0%91%e9%87%8f%e6%a0%87%e6%b3%a8-ads-b-%e4%bf%a1","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/%e5%9f%ba%e4%ba%8e%e5%b0%84%e9%a2%91%e6%8c%87%e7%ba%b9%e7%9a%84%e7%9c%9f%e5%ae%9e%e5%9c%ba%e6%99%af%e9%a3%9e%e6%9c%ba%e8%af%86%e5%88%ab%ef%bc%9a%e5%b0%91%e9%87%8f%e6%a0%87%e6%b3%a8-ads-b-%e4%bf%a1\/","title":{"rendered":"RF Fingerprint-Based Aircraft Identification in Real-World Scenarios: Methods with Few Labeled ADS-B Signals"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3749991f wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"min-height:1000px\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-458a08b5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\"><h2 class=\"lab-paper-title wp-block-post-title\">RF Fingerprint-Based Aircraft Identification in Real-World Scenarios: Methods with Few Labeled ADS-B Signals<\/h2>\n\n\n<p class=\"lab-paper-meta has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Z. Zhang, G. Li, J. Shi, H. Li, and A. Hu<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"lab-paper-meta has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology<\/em><\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons lab-btn-group is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/Real-World_Aircraft_Recognition_Based_on_RF_Fingerprinting_With_Few_Labeled_ADS-B_Signals.pdf\">\ud83d\udcc4 PDF<\/a><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-fill\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/TVT.2023.3314491\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/LWC.2023.3330809 noreferrer noopener\">\ud83d\udd17 DOI Link<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-text-color has-contrast-3-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-contrast-3-background-color has-background is-style-wide\" style=\"margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"\/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-46005010 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udccc Abstract<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote has-text-align-left lab-abstract-quote has-small-font-size\" style=\"margin-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);margin-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);padding-top:0;padding-right:0;padding-bottom:0;padding-left:0\"><blockquote><p>Automatic Dependent Surveillance-Broadcast (ADS-B) is regarded as an alternative to radar in the air transportation system; however, its lack of authentication and encryption mechanisms makes it vulnerable to attacks. This paper proposes a noise-robust RF fingerprinting method to address the practical aircraft identification scenario under small-sample conditions. We design a preprocessing method that enhances noise robustness by zero-padding invalid signals and adopt a Siamese network-based small-sample training scheme for RFF identification. The method is evaluated on a real-world ADS-B dataset, and the results show that, under small-sample conditions, signal preprocessing improves aircraft identification accuracy by approximately 20% compared to directly using raw signals; even with only dozens of labeled samples, the proposed method achieves an identification accuracy exceeding 90%, outperforming other CNN-based recognizers by more than 30%.<\/p><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-6adec98e lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udca1 Core Contributions<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<ul start=\"1\" style=\"border-style:none;border-width:0px\" class=\"wp-block-list lab-feature-list\">\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Proposes a noise-robust preprocessing method for real-world ADS-B scenarios<\/strong>: To address the issue of numerous invalid segments (e.g., noise segments beyond the preamble) in real-world collected ADS-B signals, a zero-padding-based signal preprocessing pipeline is designed to effectively suppress interference from invalid signals and significantly enhance model robustness under low-SNR conditions.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Introduces Siamese networks into the small-sample learning framework for ADS-B RF fingerprinting identification<\/strong>: A metric learning scheme based on Siamese networks is constructed, which learns the similarity between signal pairs rather than performing direct classification, enabling the model to accomplish aircraft identification under extreme small-sample conditions with only dozens of labeled samples per class, thereby resolving the dependence of traditional CNN methods on large amounts of labeled data.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Achieves comprehensive improvement over existing methods on real-world datasets<\/strong>: Systematic evaluation is conducted on a real-world large-scale ADS-B dataset, and the proposed method achieves an identification accuracy exceeding 90% under small-sample conditions, improving by more than 30% over other CNN baseline methods, thereby validating the feasibility and superiority of the method in practical deployment scenarios.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-2f9d57f4 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udd27 Method Overview<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group lab-paper-results is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-b46d2053 wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-9cfa9a5a\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png ,http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png 780w, http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-428\" width=\"802\" height=\"656\" title=\"8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-831b2db5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<p class=\"lab-experiment-caption has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">The RFF identification framework proposed in this paper consists of two core modules connected in series.<strong>Stage I<\/strong>, the raw I\/Q signals are processed by the zero-padding (ZP) preprocessing algorithm, which locates valid pulse intervals through coarse and fine synchronization, filters out low-level noise segments, and reconstructs the signals, significantly improving signal quality.<strong>Stage II<\/strong>, the preprocessed signals enter a two-stage Siamese network training scheme: first, the Siamese network is trained with signal pairs as input to obtain an RFF feature extractor, which is then fine-tuned with an MLP classifier to ultimately output aircraft identification results.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-dda34f26 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udcca Experimental Results<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group lab-paper-results is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-080de2b0 wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-9cfa9a5a\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/a3d420dd59e4354d91145054e2ab4ef2.png ,http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/a3d420dd59e4354d91145054e2ab4ef2.png 780w, http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/a3d420dd59e4354d91145054e2ab4ef2.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/a3d420dd59e4354d91145054e2ab4ef2.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-876\" width=\"802\" height=\"656\" title=\"a3d420dd59e4354d91145054e2ab4ef2\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-831b2db5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<p class=\"lab-experiment-caption has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Experiments are evaluated on a real-world collected ADS-B dataset (198 classes, totaling 13 million samples). The results show that ZP preprocessing brings an accuracy improvement of over 20% when only 10 samples per class are available, and the gain becomes more significant with fewer samples. The proposed Siamese network scheme outperforms baseline methods such as CNN, DRCN, and QGAN at any sample scale, achieving an identification accuracy of approximately 90% with only dozens of labeled samples. Furthermore, the inference speed of the Siamese + MLP combination is approximately 7 times faster than that of Siamese + KNN, making it more suitable for real-time deployment scenarios.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-e3c2d50d lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udcdd Citation<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<pre class=\"wp-block-code lab-bibtex-code has-small-font-size\"><code>@article{zhang2024realworld,\n  author    = {Zechen Zhang and Guyue Li and Jitong Shi and Haobo Li and Aiqun Hu},\n  title     = {Real-World Aircraft Recognition Based on {RF} Fingerprinting With Few Labeled {ADS-B} Signals},\n  journal   = {IEEE Transactions on Vehicular Technology},\n  volume    = {73},\n  number    = {2},\n  pages     = {2866--2871},\n  month     = feb,\n  year      = {2024},\n  doi       = {10.1109\/TVT.2023.3314491}\n}\n<\/code><\/pre>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wide\" style=\"margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"\/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div style=\"height:100px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-content-justification-space-between is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-788841da wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>In real aviation environments, obtaining a large number of labeled aircraft ADS-B signals is extremely difficult, and the signals are often subject to strong noise interference. To address this \u201csmall-sample\u201d challenge, our research group proposes a novel RF fingerprinting framework that combines zero-padding (ZP) preprocessing with a Siamese Network. By employing weight sharing and a two-stage training strategy, this method effectively mitigates overfitting and achieves high-accuracy aircraft identity authentication with limited labeled data.<\/p>","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":428,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"mypost","format":"standard","meta":{"_uag_custom_page_level_css":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[5],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-875","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-research"],"uagb_featured_image_src":{"full":["http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png",947,668,false],"thumbnail":["http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a-150x150.png",150,150,true],"medium":["http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a-300x212.png",300,212,true],"medium_large":["http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a-768x542.png",768,542,true],"large":["http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png",947,668,false],"1536x1536":["http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png",947,668,false],"2048x2048":["http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png",947,668,false],"trp-custom-language-flag":["http:\/\/localhost:10011\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/01\/8ee4ceaf-a5d5-4001-a35c-4dd5a7a5a83a.png",18,12,false]},"uagb_author_info":{"display_name":"jiushihema","author_link":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/author\/jiushihema\/"},"uagb_comment_info":0,"uagb_excerpt":"\u5728\u771f\u5b9e\u822a\u7a7a\u73af\u5883\u4e2d\uff0c\u83b7\u53d6\u5927\u91cf\u6709\u6807\u7b7e\u7684\u98de\u673a ADS-B \u4fe1\u53f7\u6781\u5176\u56f0\u96be\uff0c\u4e14\u4fe1\u53f7\u5e38\u53d7\u5f3a\u566a\u58f0\u5e72\u6270\u3002\u9488\u5bf9\u8fd9\u4e00\u201c\u5c0f\u6837\u672c\u201d\u96be\u9898&hellip;","_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/875","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=875"}],"version-history":[{"count":21,"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/875\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":993,"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/875\/revisions\/993"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=875"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=875"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/localhost:10011\/en\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=875"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}